<title>THAILAND: Thai rice vessels loading and movements at Mar 25.</title>
<headline>Thai rice vessels loading and movements at Mar 25.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai Commerce Ministry and</p>
<p>independent surveyors detailed rice loading at Thai ports as</p>
<p>follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel		Date of Arrival   Quantity     Destination</p>
<p>Pacific Sakti     03/03/97		5,000	  Vietnam</p>
<p>Bang Kanatee	05/03/97		7,200	  Malaysia</p>
<p>Donnai		05/03/97		8,000	  Philippines</p>
<p>Golden Faith	06/03/97		1,200	  China</p>
<p>Orient Leader     07/03/97		3,500	  India</p>
<p>Ocen Leader	 07/03/97		4,000	  Hong Kong</p>
<p>Saengthai Venus   07/03/97		2,400	  Singapore</p>
<p>Pacific Concore   07/03/97		8,500	  India</p>
<p>Bang Khunnon	10/03/97		6,200	  Malaysia</p>
<p>Saengthai Khanni  12/03/97		5,200	  Singapore</p>
<p>Saengthai Ceramic 13/03/97		4,000	  Singapore</p>
<p>Kwan Mo Bong	13/03/97		8,000	  India</p>
<p>Dibena Joy	  14/03/97		6,300	  India</p>
<p>Bang Khunsri	14/03/97		5,500	  Malaysia</p>
<p>Hejikng	     14/03/97		4,800	  China</p>
<p>Saengthai Even    17/03/97		5,000	  Hong Kong</p>
<p>Fixed Star	  17/03/97	     12,500	  Iraq</p>
<p>Saengthai Timber  18/03/97		3,500	  Singapore</p>
<p>Meng Long	   18/03/97		3,700	  China</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
